      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "what-is-kafka-consumer-api",
          "heading": "What is Kafka Consumer API?",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Kafka Consumer API is part of the Kafka client library that allows applications to:"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Subscribe to one or more Kafka topics.",
                "Read and process streams of records.",
                "Work with offsets, partitions, and consumer groups."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 34,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "kafka-console-consumer-default-utility",
      "heading": "Kafka Console Consumer (Default Utility)",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "definition",
          "heading": "Definition:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "A command-line tool provided by Kafka to consume and print messages from a specified topic."
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 15,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "example-command",
          "heading": "Example Command:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "bash",
              "code": "bin/kafka-console-consumer.sh --zookeeper localhost:2181 --topic CleansedYouBuyyClickStreamData --from-beginning",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 0,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "notes",
          "heading": "Notes:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "-from-beginning ensures all past messages are consumed.",
                "This is useful for testing and verifying data on a topic."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 18,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "custom-kafka-consumer-application-java",
      "heading": "Custom Kafka Consumer Application (Java)",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "You can write custom logic using Java Kafka client libraries to process messages and extract metadata."
